A raw_text or analysed_text object with literal_parts_json holds a JSON string representing exact OCR text parts. Decode that JSON string as a list, then concatenate its parts: strings are literal; {repeat: text, count: N} contributes the exact text N times; {integer_sequence: {start, count, suffix}} contributes count successive integers starting at start, each followed by the exact suffix. The ordinary literal_parts list has the same meaning without the JSON-string decoding step.

This is reversible transport encoding, not corrected or missing text and not an instruction printed in the document. Read the represented text as evidence. Repetition alone does not prove a structural error. Never invent source characters or confuse these encoding objects with document structure.
